[28.2662, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[6B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m\u276f \u001b[38;5;231mA creator wrote this sponsored video script for Tallyleaf. Before it goes to the brand, review it\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mwith Verdict. Work only in this folder. Read sponsor-review-strict.yaml and call the verdict \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mMCP's create_rubric with its YAML. Then evaluate it with subject name \"Small Desk Studio script\",\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231ma file input script.md (tags [\"script\"]), a file input brief.json (tags [\"brief\"]) and a file \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231minput notes.json (tags [\"notes\"]). Edit only script.md. Keep the creator's voice, and say nothing\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mabout their month that isn't in notes.json. If it isn't approved, pick one failing criterion, \u001b[39m    \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mfix only that, and evaluate again. If its gate failed, fix the gate first. One fix per round, so \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mit's clear what changed the score. Stop when it's approved, or after 10 evaluations. Finally \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mprint a REVIEW table (round, score, grade, what changed).\u001b[39m                                         \r\u001b[4B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;174m\u2722\u001b[3GS\u001b[38;5;216mimm\u001b[38;5;174mering\u2026 \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;244m\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25