[101.1867, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[38;5;246m  \u23bf \u00a0\u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m line, removed \u001b[1m1\u001b[30G\u001b[22mli\u001b[34G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m  6 \u001b[22m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m  7 \u001b[22m [0:10] Day one: I connected my cards and Tallyleaf sorted my spending into categori\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m es in about a minute.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m  8 \u001b[22m \u001b[12G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m\u001b[48;5;52m  9 -\u001b[38;5;231m[0:20] The first surprise was subscriptions: four of them, $47 a month, and I'd for\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;167m    -\u001b[38;5;231mgotten two.                                                                        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m\u001b[48;5;22m  9 +\u001b[38;5;231m[0:20] The first surprise was subscriptions: four of them, $47 a month, and I'd for\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m    +\u001b[38;5;231mgotten two. Tallyleaf flags each one the day before it renews, so when those alerts\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;77m    +\u001b[38;5;231m came in I cancelled the two I'd forgotten. That's $19 a month.                    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[2m 10 \u001b[22m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 11 \u001b[22m [0:28] My roommate Jess and I set a $400 grocery budget. We both see the same numbe\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m r, and it updates when either of us pays.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[2m 12 \u001b[22m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246mCalled verdict \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;231m\u25cf\u001b[3G\u001b[39mNext: drawback\u001b[18G\u2014\u001b[20Gadd\u001b[24Gthe\u001b[28Greal\u001b[33Gones\u001b[38Gfrom\u001b[43Gnotes.json.